      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The War Eagle Mill in Hindsville is the fourth mill on the site since 1832, surviving fires and floods.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://madisoncountydirectory.com/community/hindsville/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lake Hindsville, built in March 1950, was the first reservoir constructed in Arkansas before Lake Conway was commissioned.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hindsville%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every October, Hindsville hosts the War Eagle Craft Fair, drawing hundreds of artisan vendors from across the country.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://madisoncountydirectory.com/community/hindsville/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "War Eagle Creek and its tributaries offer some of the county's most scenic views, with local outfitters guiding visitors.",
